          <section class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set" id="setup" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set-h2">
            <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__container">
              <header class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__header">
                <h2 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__h2" id="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set-h2">
                  Connect in under a minute, no developer needed
                </h2>
                <p class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__sub">
                  The native integration handles the connection in a few clicks. No Zapier subscription, no webhook JSON
                  to map, no middleware to maintain.
                </p>
              </header>

              <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__grid">
                <article class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__card">
                  <span class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
                  <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__h3">Open the monday.com integration in Formester</h3>
                  <p class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__body">
                    In your Formester form's Integrations tab, find monday.com in the integration list and click
                    Connect. Sign into your monday account in the popup, authorize Formester, and pick the board and
                    group where new items should land.
                  </p>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__visual" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-set__int-row">
