    <section class="page-component-item">
      <div class="raw-html-content">
        <div class="raw-html-embed">
          <section class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq" aria-labelledby="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq-h2">
            <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__container">
              <header class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__header">
                <h2 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h2" id="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq-h2">Common questions</h2>
              </header>

              <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__list">
                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">Why use the native integration over Zapier or a webhook?</h3>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      The native integration ships inside Formester. A few clicks, one minute, no per-task fees, no JSON
                      mapping, no middleware to maintain. Zapier costs around $20 to $40 per month for moderate volume
                      and adds a 1-to-15-minute delay on free tiers. A raw webhook is free but you write and maintain
                      the JSON-to-monday field mapping yourself. The native integration does the same job, faster to set
                      up, with no recurring cost or code.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>

                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">Do I need a paid monday plan?</h3></summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      monday's free plan caps boards and integrations. Most form-to-board flows need monday's Standard
                      plan ($12/seat) or higher for unlimited boards and integration runs. Check your current limits
                      before connecting. Full monday pricing at
                      <a href="https://monday.com/pricing/">monday.com/pricing</a>.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>

                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">What happens to file uploads?</h3></summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      Files attach to the monday File / Files column directly on the item. The recruiter or PM sees the
                      resume, contract, or asset on the item without leaving monday.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>

                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">Can it update an existing item instead of creating a new one?</h3>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      Yes, with a unique-identifier field (email, submission ID, or a custom field). Set the mapping to
                      "Update if match found, else create." Useful for re-submissions, edits, and forms behind a
                      logged-in portal.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>

                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary>
                    <h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">Will it slow down the form submission for the user?</h3>
                  </summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      No. The post-to-monday step runs asynchronously after the respondent sees the thank-you page. A
                      delay or failure on monday's side never blocks the form from submitting on Formester's side.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>

                <details class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__item">
                  <summary><h3 class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__h3">How do I test before going live?</h3></summary>
                  <div class="fmstr-cmp-mdy-faq__answer">
                    <p>
                      Connect to a sandbox board, submit a test response, verify it lands correctly, then point the
                      integration at the live board. Submissions log inside Formester so you can replay any failed send.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                </details>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

